            <title>[LU-20813] sanity test_160g: intermittent "user2 index expected N, but is N+1"</title>
                <link>https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-20813</link>
                <project id="10000" key="LU">Lustre</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;sanity test_160g sometimes fails with:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;  mds1: user2 cl9 index  expected 24, but is 25&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;This is a test race, not a product bug.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The test calls changelog_register twice in a row. Each registration sets the new user's&lt;br/&gt;
ndex to the MDT's current changelog index (rec-&amp;gt;cur_endrec = mdd-&amp;gt;mdd_cl.mc_index in&lt;br/&gt;
mdd_changelog_user_register()). Later the test checks that user1 and user2 have&lt;br/&gt;
the same index ([ $user_rec1 == $user_rec2 ]).&lt;br/&gt;
                                                                                      &lt;br/&gt;
This only holds if no changelog record is written between the two register calls. If one&lt;br/&gt;
record lands in that window, user2 starts one ahead of user1 and stays one ahead. That's&lt;br/&gt;
why the difference is always exactly 1.&lt;br/&gt;
 &lt;br/&gt;
changelog_user_rec reads the user's own index (cur_endrec), and only a changelog clear&lt;br/&gt;
moves it. So the race is in the two registrations, not around __changelog_clear.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Possible fix: read both users' indexes right after registering and compare the changes&lt;br/&gt;
(deltas), not the absolute values. Or make sure no changelog activity happens between the&lt;br/&gt;
two registrations.&lt;br/&gt;
 &lt;br/&gt;
Seen on: Gerrit 68095 PS22, Janitor build 70480, sanity2@ldiskfs+DNE. Janitor also listed&lt;br/&gt;
it in reviews 67745, 65414, 65183 and 62952, so it doesn't come from one patch.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
